  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The flat roof area(s) of the development to which this permission relates shall not be used as a roof garden, balcony, seating area or other similar amenity area, and shall not be accessed except for the purpose of maintenance or in the case of emergency.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Prior to the commencement of any development above ground level, details of secure cycle parking facilities to serve the development to which this permission relates shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rThe cycle parking facilities as shown in the approved details shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure that appropriate opportunities to promote sustainable transport are taken up, in accordance with policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS6 and DM8 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The approved outbuilding and nail salon use shall remain strictly ancillary to the host dwellinghouse and must not be operated as an independent commercial premises or occupied as a separate residential or commercial unit. \r\rReason: The acceptability of the development depends entirely upon its restricted, ancillary nature, as the introduction of an independent commercial use or alternative uses permitted by the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 would be unlikely to be acceptable in planning terms and could harm local residential amenity.",
    "The nail salon to which this permission relates shall not open outside of the following hours:\r\r10:00 to 15:00 on Monday to Fridays \rClosed on Saturdays\rClosed on Sundays and bank holidays\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The nail salon use hereby permitted shall be limited to serving a maximum of two clients per day, and shall not exceed a maximum of six clients in any single week. \r\rReason: To ensure the commercial activity remains of a low scale and intensity that is genuinely ancillary to the host dwellinghouse, and to safeguard the residential amenity and living conditions of neighbouring occupiers from unacceptable noise, disturbance, and transport impacts, in accordance with policies DM10 and DM18 of the Kingston Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
